.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Metric | A number measured over time | `telemetry_ingest_total` |
    | Scrape | Prometheus reading a service's `/metrics` | Every few seconds |
    | Alert rule | "Fire when this number looks bad" | `ServiceDown` |
    | Trace | One request followed across services | Not built |
    | cAdvisor | Built-in container stats on each node | CPU per pod |

How a problem gets noticed, and what stays invisible.

---

## The short version

| Signal | State |
|---|---|
| Metrics | 6 of 11 backend services |
| Alert rules | Yes, but they tell nobody |
| Logs | Each service's stdout, not collected |
| Traces | None across services. `agent` alone sends LLM traces to Langfuse |

---

## Who exposes what

All six use the Rust `prometheus` crate.

| Service | Measures |
|---|---|
| `telemetry` | `telemetry_ingest_total`, persist failures, publish outcomes, `telemetry_http_*` |
| `digital-twin` | `http_requests_total`, `http_error_requests_total`, `http_request_duration_seconds` |
| `notification` | Same three names |
| `chat` | `chat_http_*` |
| `dashboard` | `telemetry_fanout_latency_ms`, events in and out |
| `socket` | Messages relayed, skipped, connections refused, clients connected |

No metrics at all: `agent`, `claims-gateway`, `tenancy`, `registry`, `provisioner`.

HTTP metrics label the route template, never the real URL, so ids cannot explode the series.

---

## Local vs cluster settings

Each environment has its own Prometheus and Grafana: compose starts one pair locally, the cluster runs another. Only one pair runs at a time. Their settings differ:

| | Local | Cluster |
|---|---|---|
| Config | `prometheus.yml`, `prometheus.rules.yml` | `k8s/monitoring/prometheus.yml` |
| Finds targets | Fixed list | Pods annotated `prometheus.io/scrape` |
| Reach it | `/prometheus/`, `/grafana/` | `/grafana` only |
| History | Image default | 15 days, 5 Gi |

The cluster also scrapes what no code exposes:

| Job | Shows |
|---|---|
| `kubernetes-cadvisor` | CPU, memory, disk of every pod, the only signal covering all services |
| `istiod` | Control plane health, certificates |
| `istio-ztunnel` | mTLS proxy stats per node |
| `istio-ingress-gateway` | Requests at the edge |

---

## Alert rules

| Alert | Fires when |
|---|---|
| `ServiceDown` | A target stops answering |
| `TwinServiceHighErrorRate`, `ChatServiceHighErrorRate`, `SensorServiceHighErrorRate` | Over 5% errors |
| `TwinServiceHighLatency`, `ChatServiceHighLatency`, `SensorServiceHighLatency` | p95 over 1 s |
| `ContractsServiceFanoutLatencyHigh` | p95 fan-out over 500 ms |
| `SensorIngestPersistFailures` | Readings fail to save |
| `SensorIngestStalled` | No accepted reading in 10 min |
| `SensorTelemetryFanoutFailing` | Publishing fails |

The queries name no job, so one rule set fits both stacks. They work because a metric name normally belongs to one service.

**Trap:** in the cluster `digital-twin` and `notification` share metric names, so the Twin rules really add up both services.

---

## Gaps

- **Nobody gets told.** No Alertmanager, so an alert only shows on Prometheus's page.
- **Rules are copied by hand** between the two stacks, and have drifted: the cluster still has `NodeEventLoopLagHigh`, for Node services that no longer exist.
- **Local misses `notification`:** it is not in `prometheus.yml`.
- **No alert yet** on `socket`'s `relay_messages_skipped_total` or `socket_connections_rejected_total`, nor on `notification`'s dead-letter topic.
- **Control plane is invisible:** a failing sign-in shows nowhere.
